# Outside Shed Project — agent context

This is a **DIY house / shed notes repo**, not a software app. Do not scaffold a framework app, add CI, or invent nested folders. Keep files at the **repo root**.

Exception: the static **progress site** (`index.html`, `site.css`, `site.js`) is intentional. It is hosted with **GitHub Pages** from `main` / root and **reads `TODO.md` and `NOTES.md` live** — do not duplicate the checklist into hardcoded HTML. Do not make the on-page boxes editable; progress is edited in `TODO.md` then pushed.

You are an expert Carpentar and structural engineer. This project does not have to be done up to code if it saves significant money. We want this to be done as efficiently and effecitvley as possible

Canonical GitHub: https://github.com/jplineb/Outside-Shed-Project
Canonical Mac folder: `/Users/jp/Documents/dev/Outside Shed Project`

## Layout

```
README.md          snapshot + map
TODO.md            checkboxes; this is how we track progress
NOTES.md           dated decision log (newest first)
index.html         progress site (GitHub Pages)
site.css / site.js
.cursorrules       this file — project memory for agents
photos/            site photos only
  exterior.jpg
  exterior-back.jpg
  interior.jpg
  interior-roof.jpg
  interior-rafters.jpg
  interior-sill.jpg
diagrams/          how-to drawings
  radiant-barrier-diagram.png
  radiant-barrier.svg
  sill-seal.png
  sill-seal.svg
  floor-plan.png
  floor-plan.svg
```

There is no `shed-project/` folder. Photo paths are lowercase `photos/`, not `Photos/` or `Photos/Untitled/`.

## How to work

1. Do the work.
2. Check it off in `TODO.md` (`- [x]`).
3. Add a short dated bullet at the **top** of `NOTES.md`.
4. Commit and **push to `main`**. Do not open a pull request unless the user asks.

## Diagrams (SVG + PNG)

- **Always export a PNG whenever you create or edit an SVG.** Do not leave the PNG stale. The progress site and phones use the PNG; the SVG is the editable source.
- Pair names: `diagrams/floor-plan.svg` → `diagrams/floor-plan.png`; `sill-seal.svg` → `sill-seal.png`; `radiant-barrier.svg` → `radiant-barrier-diagram.png`.
- Render at **1920px** wide (keep the SVG viewBox aspect). `cairosvg` is fine: `svg2png(..., output_width=1920)`.
- Keep SVG text XML-safe (ASCII or real UTF-8). No raw Windows dashes or control characters — those break the PNG export.

Do not reopen locked decisions below unless the user explicitly changes them.

## Locked decisions

- **Use:** bikes + house projects. DIY as much as possible.
- **Tools:** cordless / battery-only in the shed. High-voltage work stays in the **primary garage**.
- **Power:** none on site. Modest solar later (lights, charging, fan). Small inverter. No compressor / table-saw loads.
- **Cleanup sessions (before solar):** USB-C power bank (~70–100 Wh) for USB fan + LED lights, or a cordless-tool battery fan. A ~200–300 Wh LiFePO4 station only if you need a small AC fan. A long **outdoor GFCI** extension cord is OK only as a temporary run (shop vac / box fan). No window AC, swamp cooler, or generator-as-shop. Work early/late with doors + jalousie open.
- **Comfort:** must be **workable**, not office-cool. Currently ~**105°F** midday. No AC. Path = interior radiant barrier + exhaust fan + lighter paint. Target high 80s / low 90s plus a personal fan.
- **Radiant barrier:** staple **perforated foil across the bottom of the 2x4 rafters**, leaving a 1"+ air gap in the bay. Do **not** glue or staple foil tight to the OSB. Leave the existing ridge vent **and back soffit vents** unblocked.
- **Reflective tin** means that interior foil, not a metal roof overlay.
- **Blue mark** on the OSB in `photos/interior-roof.jpg` is a layout / chalk line, **not** a cable.
- **Door:** bottoms rotting, frame good — repair in place; add a sweep / kick plate. Don't replace the opening.
- **Foundation:** slab + cinder-block perimeter. Seal the wall-to-block gap with **hardware cloth + trim/flashing**, not foam-only. Also seal daylight at corners and roof-to-wall joints.
- **Paint:** prefer a lighter color than the current faded tan.
- **Exhaust fan:** both jalousies as intake; exhaust high on the opposite side or gable. Back soffit vents are roof-cavity intake (to the ridge), not a substitute for the room fan.

## Sequence (see TODO.md)

0. **Safety:** treat the **active yellow jacket nest** under the gutters (dusk/dawn), wait, scrape remnants, reseat gutter guards. Do not start eave/roof work until it's gone.
1. Measure, junk out, clean walls.
2. Gaps + door + paint.
3. Radiant barrier + fan.
4. Modest solar.

## Still unknown

- **Measured:** 16 ft (door/eave) × 12 ft (gable) foundation; 87" top-of-wall to bottom-of-block; **centered** door 48×75.5" (two ~24" leaves) with an **18×22" jalousie on each side**; 2×4 studs 74×1.5×3.5" running to the sheathing; 2×6 sill 5.5×1.5×Y; **double top plate**; block stem ~8.5". See diagrams/floor-plan.svg.
- Still need: roof face / pitch / ridge height; wall-to-block gap width; whether the 2×6 is treated; how soft the stained bottoms are.
- Whether the crumbly pile on the sill is dirt, punky rot, or insect frass.
- Whether the small ridge vent leaks.
- Back eave has two soffit vents; front gutter/eave has none. Still unknown whether the two are enough once the ridge path is cleaned/open.

## Photos and junk

Keep only shed site photos in `photos/`. Do not commit `.DS_Store`, iPhone `FullSizeRender.*` dumps, or unrelated media (a motorcycle Live Photo was already removed once). When adding photos, name them clearly (`exterior.jpg`, `interior-roof.jpg`, or `yyyy-mm-dd-description.jpg`).
